-------------------------------------------------------------
 Kitty keybinds  ·  Doomslayer  ·  prefix = Ctrl+K

 HOW: press Ctrl+K, RELEASE it, then the action key.
      (Not a chord — same idea as tmux prefix / Ghostty Ctrl+G.)

 Ctrl+K ?         command palette (search actions/binds)
 Ctrl+K Ctrl+H    this cheat sheet in less (overlay)
 Esc              cancel prefix mode
-------------------------------------------------------------

  PREFIX
    Ctrl+K            enter prefix mode (one shot)
    Esc               cancel prefix mode
    k  or  Ctrl+K     send real Ctrl+K to the app (after prefix)

  TABS  (~ tmux windows)
    Ctrl+K c          new tab
    Ctrl+K n / p      next / previous tab
    Ctrl+K l / 0      last tab (previously active)
    Ctrl+K 1 … 9      go to tab N
    Ctrl+K ,          rename tab
    Ctrl+K w          select tab (interactive)
    Ctrl+K d          close whole tab (all splits in it)

  WINDOWS
    Ctrl+K Shift+c    new OS window
    Ctrl+K &          close OS window

  SPLITS  (~ tmux panes)
    Ctrl+K h          horizontal split  (left | right)
    Ctrl+K v          vertical split    (top / bottom)
    Ctrl+K %          same as h
    Ctrl+K "          same as v
    Ctrl+K ←↓↑→       focus split
    Ctrl+K R          resize MODE (then arrows/hjkl; Esc exits)
    Ctrl+K Ctrl+←…→   one-shot resize
    Ctrl+K Shift+hjkl focus split (vim)
    Ctrl+K o / ;      next / previous split
    Ctrl+K z          zoom / unzoom pane (stack layout)
    Ctrl+K =          equalize splits

  FONT ZOOM  (no prefix — same as wezterm)
    Ctrl+=  or  Ctrl++   zoom in
    Ctrl+-               zoom out
    Ctrl+0               reset font size
    Ctrl+wheel           zoom in / out

  SEARCH / SCROLL
    Ctrl+K f  or  /   scrollback pager (search with / inside)
    Ctrl+K [ / ]      page up / page down
    Ctrl+K Home / G   scroll top / bottom
    Ctrl+K a          copy whole screen to clipboard

  MISC
    Ctrl+K ?          VIEW KEYBINDS — command palette
    Ctrl+K Ctrl+H     VIEW KEYBINDS — this cheat sheet (less)

    Ctrl+K r          reload config
    Ctrl+K Enter      toggle fullscreen
    Ctrl+K i          debug config dump

  NOTES
    · Shell Ctrl+D already exits a pane (EOF) — no prefix needed.
    · Prefix+d closes the tab; prefix+& closes the OS window.
    · h/v use tmux naming: h = side-by-side, v = stacked.
    · Ghostty twin uses Ctrl+G with the same layout of binds.
